From c303a281b5fdc677c31791d7bbc576c9c60974c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:06:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Extract inline base64 logo image to a static file

The homepage HTML embedded a 65KB JPEG (Purity Collective badge logo)
directly as a base64 data URI inside an <img> tag, adding ~87KB of
base64 text to every page load. Extracted it to PC-Authorized-Logo.jpg
and reference it by path instead.

Benefits:
- Shrinks index.html from ~686KB to ~599KB
- Lets the logo be cached and reused independently instead of being
  re-downloaded (undecoded, uncacheable) with every HTML page load
- Removes a large embedded high-entropy (already-compressed-looking)
  blob from the HTML response, which is one of the leading suspects
  in the ongoing investigation into why Cloudflare's edge compression
  intermittently fails to apply to this page at the SJC colo

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U6KEFNrZj3xktuCvJvtYyw
---
 PC-Authorized-Logo.jpg | Bin 0 -> 65265 bytes
 index.html             |   2 +-
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 PC-Authorized-Logo.jpg

diff --git a/PC-Authorized-Logo.jpg b/PC-Authorized-Logo.jpg
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2551ec22cac224fec14510da28c176b238764438
GIT binary patch
